response:
To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function from the `<stdlib.h>` library. This function takes an integer argument that represents the exit status of the program.

Here's an example:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your code here

    printf("Program terminated successfully.\n");
    exit(0);  // Exit with success (status code 0)

    return 0;
}
```

In this example, after printing "Program terminated successfully.", the `exit(0)` statement is called to terminate
